# Example index file for NetCDF-format geographic source data
#
# This demonstrates how to use a NetCDF file as input to init_atmosphere
# for generating MPAS static.nc files, instead of the traditional WPS
# geogrid binary format.
#
# Place this 'index' file in a directory alongside your NetCDF data file.
# The directory path is what you specify in the GEOG_DATA_PATH.
#
# Required keywords for NetCDF format:
#   format    - must be "netcdf"
#   filename  - name of the NetCDF file (relative to this directory)
#   variable  - name of the variable to read from the NetCDF file
#   type      - "continuous" or "categorical"
#   dx, dy    - grid spacing in degrees
#   known_x, known_y  - reference pixel (usually 1.0)
#   known_lat, known_lon - lat/lon of the reference pixel center
#   tile_x, tile_y    - virtual tile size (for memory management chunking)
#   tile_z    - number of vertical levels (1 for 2D fields)
#
# Optional keywords:
#   tile_bdr      - border/halo pixels (default: 0)
#   scale_factor  - post-read multiplication factor (default: 1.0)
#   category_min, category_max - for categorical data
#   missing_value - value to treat as missing
#
# Notes:
#   - The NetCDF variable must be on a regular lat-lon grid
#   - Dimensions should be ordered (y, x) for 2D or (z, y, x) for 3D
#   - CF-convention scale_factor and add_offset attributes are applied automatically
#   - _FillValue / missing_value attributes are handled (replaced with 0)
#   - tile_x and tile_y control how much data is loaded at once (memory chunks);
#     they do NOT need to correspond to physical file structure
#
# ============================================================================
# Example: GMTED2010 terrain elevation from a single global NetCDF file
# ============================================================================
format = netcdf
filename = gmted2010_30s.nc
variable = elevation
type = continuous
projection = regular_ll
dx = 0.00833333
dy = 0.00833333
known_x = 1.0
known_y = 1.0
known_lat = -89.99583
known_lon = -179.99583
tile_x = 1200
tile_y = 1200
tile_z = 1
tile_bdr = 3
scale_factor = 1.0
